[   4.2 min] If you're looking for an alternative, you could also try grilling the chicken breasts over medium-high heat until they start to brown slightly, then transferring them to a pan with some oil and finishing them on low heat for about 10 minutes per side. This method is generally quicker than direct high heat but still allows for a good level of browning and tenderness.
